      "message": "We will need to measure the performance and see if this placement is ok because pte_shift is used quite often. Technically you need just one bit to encode 4k vs 16k. We might be able to squeeze it into the first cacheline of mm_struct but for now this is ok. What I would suggest is to create an inline helper:\n```\nstatic int u8 get_pte_shift(const struct mm_struct *mm)\n{\n    return mm-\u003econtext.pte_shift;\n}\n```\nAnd use it everywhere to access pte_shift. If we decide to change its location, we will need to only change this helper.",
