      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Suren.\n\nThe mm_context_t is embedded directly into struct mm_struct Accessing `mm-\u003econtext.pte_shift` does not introduce an extra pointer dereference it should compile to a single offset from the mm base similar  to having `mm-\u003epte_shift` directly in `mm_struct`.\n\nThe inline helper we have is `mm_pte_shift()`. This is already used as the accessor to avoid ifdefs sprinkled throughout and since we need to not affect the 4KB ABI.\n\nSo we can change it easily in a follow up if needed",
